  <entry>
    <title>PicoCTF 2026: Reverse Engineering Write-up</title>
    <link href="https://4r12u.github.io/posts/picoctf-2026-reverse-engineering/" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <id>https://4r12u.github.io/posts/picoctf-2026-reverse-engineering/</id>
    <published>2026-04-22T00:00:00.000Z</published>
    <updated>2026-04-22T00:00:00.000Z</updated>
    <summary>A collection of reverse engineering solutions from PicoCTF 2026.</summary>
    <content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>This write-up covers the PicoCTF 2026 challenges I solved with <strong>EHC_Loi_Yeu_Kho_Noi_Pl2s</strong>. It mainly focuses on reverse engineering, using IDA Pro, Ghidra, Detect It Easy, Scapy/Wireshark, and LLM-assisted analysis.</p>
<section class="markdown-section"><h2 id="gatekeeper">Gatekeeper<a class="anchor" href="https://4r12u.github.io/posts/picoctf-2026-reverse-engineering/#gatekeeper"><span class="anchor-icon" data-pagefind-ignore>#</span></a></h2><p>The program expects a number greater than 999 and less than 9999. Because it uses <code>atoi</code>, an ASCII string can be converted into a number. Testing with <code>abc</code> produces an output containing the repeated string <code>ftc_oc_ip</code>. Removing the repeated characters leaves:</p><div class="expressive-code"><figure class="frame" data-language="text"><figcaption class="header"></figcaption><pre data-language="text" class="wrap" style="--ecMaxLine:36ch"><code><div class="ec-line"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">1</div></div><div class="code"><span style="--0:#24292e;--1:#e1e4e8">}847d936b_999_TG_xeh_tigid_3{FTCocip</span></div></div></code></pre><div class="copy-btn-icon"></div></figure></div><p>Reversing each chunk gives the flag:</p><div class="expressive-code"><figure class="frame" data-language="text"><figcaption class="header"></figcaption><pre data-language="text" class="wrap" style="--ecMaxLine:36ch"><code><div class="ec-line"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">1</div></div><div class="code"><span style="--0:#24292e;--1:#e1e4e8">picoCTF{3_digit_hex_GT_999_b639d748}</span></div></div></code></pre><div class="copy-btn-icon"></div></figure></div></section>
<section class="markdown-section"><h2 id="hidden-cipher-1">Hidden Cipher 1<a class="anchor" href="https://4r12u.github.io/posts/picoctf-2026-reverse-engineering/#hidden-cipher-1"><span class="anchor-icon" data-pagefind-ignore>#</span></a></h2><p>The program prints an encoded flag:</p><div class="expressive-code"><figure class="frame" data-language="text"><figcaption class="header"></figcaption><pre data-language="text" class="wrap" style="--ecMaxLine:36ch"><code><div class="ec-line"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">1</div></div><div class="code"><span style="--0:#24292e;--1:#e1e4e8">235a201d70201548251358110c552f135409</span></div></div></code></pre><div class="copy-btn-icon"></div></figure></div><p>After inspecting the binary in IDA, XORing the encoded text with the recovered value gives:</p><div class="expressive-code"><figure class="frame" data-language="text"><figcaption class="header"></figcaption><pre data-language="text" class="wrap" style="--ecMaxLine:37ch"><code><div class="ec-line"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">1</div></div><div class="code"><span style="--0:#24292e;--1:#e1e4e8">picoCTF{xor_unpack_4nalys1s_530ca742}</span></div></div></code></pre><div class="copy-btn-icon"></div></figure></div></section>
<section class="markdown-section"><h2 id="hidden-cipher-2">Hidden Cipher 2<a class="anchor" href="https://4r12u.github.io/posts/picoctf-2026-reverse-engineering/#hidden-cipher-2"><span class="anchor-icon" data-pagefind-ignore>#</span></a></h2><p>The service first asks a simple math question and then prints an encoded flag. The decompiled encoder multiplies every flag byte by <code>a2</code>:</p><div class="expressive-code"><figure class="frame" data-language="c"><figcaption class="header"></figcaption><pre data-language="c" class="wrap" style="--ecMaxLine:31ch"><code><div class="ec-line"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">1</div></div><div class="code"><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">for</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> (i </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">=</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> </span><span style="--0:#005CC5;--1:#79B8FF">0</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">; </span><span style="--0:#AE4B07;--1:#FFAB70">flag</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">[i]; </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">++</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">i) {</span></div></div><div class="ec-line" style="--ecIndent:4ch"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">2</div></div><div class="code"><span class="indent">    </span><span style="--0:#6F42C1;--1:#B392F0">printf</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">(</span><span style="--0:#032F62;--1:#9ECBFF">"</span><span style="--0:#005CC5;--1:#79B8FF">%d</span><span style="--0:#032F62;--1:#9ECBFF">"</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">, a2 </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">*</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> </span><span style="--0:#AE4B07;--1:#FFAB70">flag</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">[i]);</span></div></div><div class="ec-line"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">3</div></div><div class="code"><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">}</span></div></div></code></pre><div class="copy-btn-icon"></div></figure></div><p>The known prefix <code>picoCTF{</code> shows that the multiplier is 15. Dividing every value by 15 and converting the results to ASCII recovers:</p><div class="expressive-code"><figure class="frame" data-language="text"><figcaption class="header"></figcaption><pre data-language="text" class="wrap" style="--ecMaxLine:36ch"><code><div class="ec-line"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">1</div></div><div class="code"><span style="--0:#24292e;--1:#e1e4e8">picoCTF{m4th_b3h1nd_c1ph3r_4a3b2ccf}</span></div></div></code></pre><div class="copy-btn-icon"></div></figure></div></section>
<section class="markdown-section"><h2 id="the-addon-trap">The Add/On Trap<a class="anchor" href="https://4r12u.github.io/posts/picoctf-2026-reverse-engineering/#the-addon-trap"><span class="anchor-icon" data-pagefind-ignore>#</span></a></h2><p>The challenge is a Firefox <code>.xpi</code> extension. Renaming it to <code>.zip</code> exposes <code>main.js</code>, which contains a Base64 key and a Fernet-encrypted webhook URL. The key is:</p><div class="expressive-code"><figure class="frame" data-language="text"><figcaption class="header"></figcaption><pre data-language="text" class="wrap" style="--ecMaxLine:44ch"><code><div class="ec-line"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">1</div></div><div class="code"><span style="--0:#24292e;--1:#e1e4e8">cGljb0NURnt5b3UncmUgb24gdGhlIHJpZ2h0IHRyYX0=</span></div></div></code></pre><div class="copy-btn-icon"></div></figure></div><p>Decrypting the webhook with Python’s <code>cryptography.fernet</code> module reveals the flag:</p><div class="expressive-code"><figure class="frame" data-language="text"><figcaption class="header"></figcaption><pre data-language="text" class="wrap" style="--ecMaxLine:36ch"><code><div class="ec-line"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">1</div></div><div class="code"><span style="--0:#24292e;--1:#e1e4e8">picoCTF{Us3_4dd/0ns_v3ry_c4r3fully1}</span></div></div></code></pre><div class="copy-btn-icon"></div></figure></div></section>
<section class="markdown-section"><h2 id="silent-stream">Silent Stream<a class="anchor" href="https://4r12u.github.io/posts/picoctf-2026-reverse-engineering/#silent-stream"><span class="anchor-icon" data-pagefind-ignore>#</span></a></h2><p>The challenge provides a PCAP and an encoder that sends each byte as <code>(byte + 42) % 256</code>. The useful TCP payloads are on port 9000. Extracting the raw bytes with Scapy and subtracting 42 reconstructs a JPEG file:</p><div class="expressive-code"><figure class="frame" data-language="python"><figcaption class="header"></figcaption><pre data-language="python" class="wrap" style="--ecMaxLine:69ch"><code><div class="ec-line"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">1</div></div><div class="code"><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">from</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> scapy.all </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">import</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> Raw, </span><span style="--0:#005CC5;--1:#79B8FF">TCP</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">, rdpcap</span></div></div><div class="ec-line"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">2</div></div><div class="code">
</div></div><div class="ec-line"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">3</div></div><div class="code"><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">packets </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">=</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> rdpcap(</span><span style="--0:#032F62;--1:#9ECBFF">"packets.pcap"</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">)</span></div></div><div class="ec-line"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">4</div></div><div class="code"><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">encoded </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">=</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> </span><span style="--0:#005CC5;--1:#79B8FF">bytearray</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">()</span></div></div><div class="ec-line"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">5</div></div><div class="code"><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">for</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> packet </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">in</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> packets:</span></div></div><div class="ec-line" style="--ecIndent:4ch"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">6</div></div><div class="code"><span class="indent">    </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">if</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> Raw </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">in</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> packet </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">and</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> </span><span style="--0:#005CC5;--1:#79B8FF">TCP</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">in</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> packet </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">and</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> packet[</span><span style="--0:#005CC5;--1:#79B8FF">TCP</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">].dport </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">==</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> </span><span style="--0:#005CC5;--1:#79B8FF">9000</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">:</span></div></div><div class="ec-line" style="--ecIndent:8ch"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">7</div></div><div class="code"><span class="indent"><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">        </span></span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">encoded.extend(packet[Raw].load)</span></div></div><div class="ec-line"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">8</div></div><div class="code">
</div></div><div class="ec-line"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">9</div></div><div class="code"><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">decoded </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">=</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> </span><span style="--0:#005CC5;--1:#79B8FF">bytes</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">((byte </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">-</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> </span><span style="--0:#005CC5;--1:#79B8FF">42</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">) </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">%</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> </span><span style="--0:#005CC5;--1:#79B8FF">256</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">for</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> byte </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">in</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> encoded)</span></div></div><div class="ec-line"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">10</div></div><div class="code"><span style="--0:#005CC5;--1:#79B8FF">open</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">(</span><span style="--0:#032F62;--1:#9ECBFF">"flag.jpeg"</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">, </span><span style="--0:#032F62;--1:#9ECBFF">"wb"</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">).write(decoded)</span></div></div></code></pre><div class="copy-btn-icon"></div></figure></div><p>The recovered flag is:</p><div class="expressive-code"><figure class="frame" data-language="text"><figcaption class="header"></figcaption><pre data-language="text" class="wrap" style="--ecMaxLine:35ch"><code><div class="ec-line"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">1</div></div><div class="code"><span style="--0:#24292e;--1:#e1e4e8">picoCTF{tr4ck_th3_tr4ff1c_8d66583c}</span></div></div></code></pre><div class="copy-btn-icon"></div></figure></div></section>
<section class="markdown-section"><h2 id="secure-password-database">Secure Password Database<a class="anchor" href="https://4r12u.github.io/posts/picoctf-2026-reverse-engineering/#secure-password-database"><span class="anchor-icon" data-pagefind-ignore>#</span></a></h2><p>The password is generated by XORing an obfuscated byte array with <code>0xAA</code> before hashing it:</p><div class="expressive-code"><figure class="frame" data-language="c"><figcaption class="header"></figcaption><pre data-language="c" class="wrap" style="--ecMaxLine:38ch"><code><div class="ec-line"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">1</div></div><div class="code"><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">for</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> (i </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">=</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> </span><span style="--0:#005CC5;--1:#79B8FF">0</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">; </span><span style="--0:#AE4B07;--1:#FFAB70">obf_bytes</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">[i]; </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">++</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">i)</span></div></div><div class="ec-line" style="--ecIndent:4ch"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">2</div></div><div class="code"><span class="indent">    </span><span style="--0:#AE4B07;--1:#FFAB70">password</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">[i] </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">=</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> </span><span style="--0:#AE4B07;--1:#FFAB70">obf_bytes</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">[i] </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">^</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8"> </span><span style="--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583">0x</span><span style="--0:#005CC5;--1:#79B8FF">AA</span><span style="--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8">;</span></div></div></code></pre><div class="copy-btn-icon"></div></figure></div><p>Recovering the bytes and reproducing the hash function produces the expected input and the flag:</p><div class="expressive-code"><figure class="frame" data-language="text"><figcaption class="header"></figcaption><pre data-language="text" class="wrap" style="--ecMaxLine:25ch"><code><div class="ec-line"><div class="gutter"><div class="ln" aria-hidden="true">1</div></div><div class="code"><span style="--0:#24292e;--1:#e1e4e8">picoCTF{d0nt_trust_us3rs}</span></div></div></code></pre><div class="copy-btn-icon"></div></figure></div></section>
<section class="markdown-section"><h2 id="notes">Notes<a class="anchor" href="https://4r12u.github.io/posts/picoctf-2026-reverse-engineering/#notes"><span class="anchor-icon" data-pagefind-ignore>#</span></a></h2><p>The original repository contains the remaining challenge files, scripts, binaries, and packet captures used during analysis. They are available in the <a href="https://github.com/4r12u/PicoCTF_WU" data-content-link-kind="external" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer">PicoCTF_WU repository</a>.</p></section>]]></content>
